00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:26.640
what does this do? Well, just imagine grabbing&nbsp;
your smartphone, taking a few images or videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.680
of real places, and then, we could create&nbsp;
a virtual version of them and play in them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:40.320
in real time. And it does exactly that. And&nbsp;
these scenes come out really really detailed.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.440
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.160
And the key thing here is that this is&nbsp;
a handcrafted technique that is easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:58.120
