00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:03.240
And it gets better. Then, we can even really&nbsp;
put these little models into our virtual worlds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:10.440
and animate them. And all this process takes…how&nbsp;
long exactly? The previous paper we looked at took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:16.360
40 minutes, so what about this one? Now&nbsp;
hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:24.800
because it is two minutes. This is incredible!&nbsp;
A 20x speedup in just one paper. I really don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.280
know what to say here. In the first step, it&nbsp;
lines up the Gaussians, little mathematical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:36.320
lumps to match the shape of the character&nbsp;
or object, and then, in the second step,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:43.200
it slowly refines the textures as well. And this&nbsp;
one runs on a single consumer graphics card, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:50.960
is what does it in two minutes per object. Haha!&nbsp;
This work is a real match for Two Minute Papers.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.920
No wonder these papers caught the imagination of&nbsp;
you Fellow Scholars. It gets even better. It can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:05.720
even reproduce photorealistic faces reasonably&nbsp;
well with just 25 photos as an input, and…whoa!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:14.240
Here, you can even animate these inputs. So not&nbsp;
only creating virtual worlds from the real world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:23.440
but we can even let our imagination run wild and&nbsp;
create absolutely anything out of it. I love it.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.080
Now, just one more thing. I know some&nbsp;
of you Fellow Scholars are asking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.600
okay but what is Gaussian Splatting? What&nbsp;
does that even mean? Now the Gaussian part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:40.920
means that objects in this scene will be&nbsp;
represented as a sum of many little waves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:46.640
And splatting is a way of throwing these&nbsp;
little waves from the 3D virtual world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:52.360
at our 2D screen and computing what they&nbsp;
should really look like. And this simple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.360 --> 00:05:00.640
but effective idea taking the world by storm.&nbsp;
A handcrafted technique. Powered not by AI, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:08.560
by human ingenuity. Once again, the papers coming&nbsp;
alive in the real world. What a time to be alive!

